  "question": {
    "text": "An ice cube of dimensions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> is placed in an insulation box of wall thickness <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The box keeping the ice cube at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> of temperature is brought to a room of temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The rate of melting of ice is approximately: (Latent heat of fusion of ice is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and thermal conducting of insulation wall is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>05</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"
  },
